%H A099155 Frank Harary, John P. Hayes, and Horng-Jyh Wu, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/0898-1221(88)90213-1">A survey of the theory of hypercube graphs</a>, Comput. Math. Appl. 15(4) (1988), 277-289.
%H A099155 Simon Hood, Daniel Recoskie, Joe Sawada, and Dennis Wong, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s10878-013-9630-z">Snakes, coils, and single-track circuit codes with spread k</a>, J. Combin. Optim. 30(1) (2015), 42-62. See Table 2 (lower bounds for n<=17).
%H A099155 Krys J. Kochut, <a href="https://combinatorialpress.com/jcmcc-articles/volume-020/snake-in-the-box-codes-for-dimension-7/">Snake-In-The-Box Codes for Dimension 7</a>, J. Combin. Math. Combin. Comput. 20 (1996), 175-185.
%H A099155 Tim Kunt, Thorsten Koch, and Hyejun Park, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.25268">Integer Programming Strategies for the Snake-in-the-Box Problem</a>, arXiv:2611.25268 [math.OC], 2026.
%H A099155 Randall Munroe, <a href="https://xkcd.com/3125/">Snake-in-the-Box Problem</a>, xkcd Web Comic #3125, Aug 06 2025.
